{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The stale-material message omits the checkbox note on its PRIMARY path\n\n`material_diff.CHECKBOX_NOTE` is introduced with this comment:\n\n    #: The advice every material-staleness reason carries, because it is the single most\n    #: frequently mis-believed fact about the gate (bug 94a3, observations 1 and 3).\n\nIt is not carried by every reason. `explain_material_change` emits it on only TWO branches:\n\n  * material_diff.py:301 — the \"no material component differs\" branch (an attestation that\n    predates AC-checkbox normalization);\n  * material_diff.py:323 — the degraded branch (an attestation that predates component-level\n    fingerprinting).\n\nThe PRIMARY branch — `delta = describe_delta(signed, current); if delta is not None: return\ndelta` (material_diff.py:295-297) — returns the named delta with NO note. That is the branch\na current attestation takes, so it is the one almost every author actually sees.\n\n## Observed\nClosing task b2bb after ticking its ACs *and* appending evidence prose to each AC item\nproduced, verbatim:\n\n    plan-review close gate: stale-material: the plan was materially edited since review —\n    changed: description (8208 -> 8829 chars). Health: current (no related material)\n    (enforced); phase planning -> execution (compatible)\n    Run rebar review-plan b2bb-fa81-e054-4fb5 separately, then retry close.\n\nNo checkbox note. The author had just been REQUIRED by the close precheck to tick boxes, so\nthe tick is the salient recent edit and the natural (wrong) conclusion is that ticking staled\nthe review. That is exactly the misconception bug 94a3 recorded three agents making; this one\nmade a fourth, with the preventing sentence present in the codebase but not on this path.\n\n## This is a MESSAGE defect, not a gate defect\nThe gate is correct and its behaviour should not change:\n  * ticking `- [ ]` -> `- [x]` is normalized out of the fingerprint and is attestation-SAFE;\n  * editing the TEXT of an acceptance criterion IS a change to the plan and SHOULD require a\n    fresh review. That is the point of binding the material.\nOnly the explanation is deficient, and only on the branch that matters most.\n\n## Secondary: the delta names the component but not what moved inside it\n`changed: description (8208 -> 8829 chars)` identifies WHICH basis key changed, not what\nwithin it. An author who ticked boxes AND edited prose in one `rebar edit` cannot tell from\nthe message which of the two is responsible — the char delta is consistent with both.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The named-delta branch of `explain_material_change` carries `CHECKBOX_NOTE` too, so\n      every `stale-material` reason states that a tick is never the cause. (The module\n      comment already claims this is true; make it true.)\n- [ ] When the changed component is `description`, the message distinguishes \"checkbox state\n      changed as well\" from \"item text changed\" — enough for the author to know which edit\n      staled the attestation, without printing the diff.\n- [ ] Held-out test: a description edit that ONLY flips checkbox state yields no staleness; an\n      edit that changes AC item text yields `stale-material` AND a reason containing the\n      checkbox note.\n\n## NOT part of this ticket — the documentation is adequate\nAn earlier draft of this bug claimed the docs fail to tell an author to record AC evidence in\na COMMENT rather than in the AC text. That claim was withdrawn on review: the guidance is\nalready present and sufficient.\n  * `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md:209` shows evidence recorded as a ticket\n    comment;\n  * `:304` states that comments are non-material and do not stale an attestation;\n  * the completion verifier's own failure text instructs the author to \"add a comment to this\n    ticket that documents the concrete artifacts\".\nAnnotating AC text with evidence instead is an author error, not a doc gap, and editing that\ntext SHOULD stale the review because it changes the plan. Nothing here asks for a doc change.\n\n## Provenance\nHit while closing b2bb during the store/signing remediation. Cross-references bug 94a3\n(the three prior agents) and bug 330c (the normalization that makes ticking safe).\n\n## Implementation plan\nAll changes in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py` (+ manifest feed), message text\nonly — no gate outcome changes.\n\n1. **AC1 — note on the primary branch.** In `explain_material_change`, the\n   `delta is not None` early return gains the same `CHECKBOX_NOTE` tail the other two\n   branches already carry, so every `stale-material` reason states that a tick is never the\n   cause.\n2. **AC2 — say what moved inside `description`.** Box state is normalized out of the signed\n   component hash, so the signed side carries no box information today. Add a DIAGNOSTIC\n   (non-basis) component `description_boxes` = (hash of the checkbox-state sequence, number\n   ticked), emitted alongside the existing `material-part:` lines. It is NOT a basis key: it\n   is absent from `COMPONENT_ORDER`, so `describe_delta` ignores it, the composite\n   fingerprint is untouched, and `material_components` keeps returning exactly the basis\n   keys (asserted by `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py:81`). A new helper\n   feeds `reviewed_material_parts` / `_current_components` the basis PLUS the diagnostic.\n3. When `description` is among the changed components, the message appends whether the\n   checkbox state also changed (with a ticked count delta) or is unchanged; when the\n   attestation predates the diagnostic line, the clause is omitted (graceful degradation,\n   same posture as the existing degraded branch). No ticket content is ever printed.\n\n## Verification\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py` gains held-out cases:\n  a description edit that ONLY flips box state produces NO staleness (composite unchanged);\n  an edit to AC item text produces a delta whose reason contains `CHECKBOX_NOTE` and the\n  text-vs-box discrimination; an old (pre-diagnostic) manifest still explains without it.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `pytest tests/unit/plan_review/` all green.\n\n## File impact\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786516707300212001,"uuid":"3951bfc7-b633-4b76-bb09-5f53d457735c"}